   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the authorization for imposition of additional sales tax in the county of Cortland",
    "basePrintNo": "S3413",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S3413-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §1210, Tax L",
    "lawSection": "Tax Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3413\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the tax law, in relation to extending the\nauthorization for imposition of additional sales tax in the county of\nCortland\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo authorize the Cortland County Legislature to continue an additional\n1 percent sales tax for a 2 year period.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThe bill amends section 1210 of the tax law, as amended by chapter 248\nof the laws of 2011, to extend the authorization for Cortland County\nto impose an additional 1 percent sales tax until November 30, 2017.\n\nEXISTING LAW:\n\nThe law is set to expire on November 30, 2015.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Cortland County Legislature passed a resolution (No.25-15)\nrequesting that the New York State Legislature introduce and pass a\nbill to authorize the county to impose an additional 1 percent sales\nand use tax for the period through November 30, 2017.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nThe law was previously extended by Chapter 226 of the laws of 2013.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediately.\n\n",
